ID: vr-19
Title: Deferred custom avatar performance and acceptance qualification
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/18

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: A reproducible candidate handoff with explicit visual and speech gates.
Dependencies: vr-18

Purpose:
DEFERRED until an owner-resumed custom-avatar implementation exists. Establish
whether it preserves the intended beauty, articulation and fluid local display.
Do not treat a rendered GLB, lower polygon count or passing automation as owner
approval. Publishing a new asset/release is a separate future authorization.

Tasks:
[ ] 19.1 Re-identify source/asset/adapter versions and define stable-use versus
    test profiles, mutable data, caches and exclusive resources. Use synthetic
    lines and owned desktop fixtures; never drive/capture unrelated apps.
[ ] 19.2 Run focused unit and real-browser regressions for both identities,
    materials, framing modes, gaze, all XYZ axes and speech playback/seek/
    pause/restart. Include missing/corrupt assets, rapid switch, cancellation,
    stale results, audio failures, context loss and clean process/profile exit.
[ ] 19.3 Measure browser/native frame-time distributions at stated CSS sizes,
    actual raster resolutions/densities, hair/edge settings and both extents.
    Record draw/normal/morph work, allocations and memory behavior where
    measured. Use existing comparable budgets or justify changes explicitly;
    retain failed runs and do not infer speedup from triangle counts alone.
[ ] 19.4 Optimize demonstrated bottlenecks while preserving reviewed identity:
    localized facial updates, cached topology, bounded GPU storage, LODs or
    material density tradeoffs as justified. Recheck affected behavior and
    show the actual fidelity/resolution tradeoff after each meaningful change.
[ ] 19.5 Review neutral front/profiles/three-quarter, hair, eye coverage,
    lips, makeup and overlay alpha with the owner. Record approval/rejection;
    technical geometry checks are not a beauty or likeness score.
[ ] 19.6 Independently review audible output and visible P/B/M closure,
    F/V contact, vowel contrasts, silence, coarticulation and expressions.
    Separate synchronization from phonetic/human accuracy; document failures,
    unsupported anatomy/languages and any explicit owner scope concessions.
[ ] 19.7 Produce actual runtime PNG/GIF evidence with source/asset provenance,
    correct sampling/density disclosures and no reference-photo substitution.
    Keep private source art, recordings and restricted assets out of output.
[ ] 19.8 Update book, guide, TODOs, causal ledger and issue/Project evidence.
    Record remaining gates and recovery instructions, not a generic success.
[ ] 19.9 Hand off an opt-in candidate and reversible return to Claire. Only
    after separate owner authorization and rights clearance prepare any new
    asset distribution, default switch or immutable source release; never move
    prototype.1/2 or imply this plan authorizes publication/deployment.

Acceptance criteria:
Reproducible evidence identifies actual versions, display workloads and failed
runs. Current Claire controls/privacy/lifecycle remain intact. Performance,
visual likeness, audible listening and articulation are separate recorded gates.
The final handoff explicitly states pass/fail/unreviewed for each; unresolved
required gates keep readiness blocked, not falsely accepted. No universal60fps,
perfect-expression or unearned human-approval claim. No automatic release,
default replacement, asset upload, service activation or deployment.

Completion evidence:
Planning only; no custom-avatar browser/native, performance or human acceptance
qualification has been performed. Earlier Claire tests and the static GLB audit
are not substitute evidence for this future candidate.

Completion log:
2026-11-19 - Future qualification/handoff work recorded as explicitly deferred.
No runtime, media gallery, release or deployed default changed.
